          "id": "pattern-1",
          "title": "Family ownership with 的 (de)",
          "explanation_en": "Use 的 (de) after a possessor when emphasizing whose person or thing it is. In close family relationships 的 is often omitted in natural speech.",
          "formula_en": "person + 的 + noun",
          "examples": [
            {
              "hanzi": "这是我的哥哥。",
              "pinyin": "Zhè shì wǒ de gēge.",
              "english": "This is my older brother."
            },
            {
              "hanzi": "我妈妈在家。",
              "pinyin": "Wǒ māma zài jiā.",
              "english": "My mom is at home."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "pattern-2",
          "title": "Introducing a relationship",
          "explanation_en": "是 (shì) identifies someone; 有 (yǒu) tells what people or things someone has. Keep the predicates distinct.",
          "formula_en": "X 是 Y / X 有 Y",
          "examples": [
